FEAST EXAMPLE:     -Selected examples for Fortran and C are provided in this directory

    !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
    !!!!Please correct accordingly compiler and libraries paths, change compiler options  in file make.inc !!!!
    !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! 

                  -Note that a F90 compiler is needed to compile the Fortan examples provided here
                   (However, all feast drivers are compatible with F77 calling interfaces and drivers can
                    be easily rewritten in F77)
                  
                  -The examples deal with two systems: system1 (a real symmetric generalized eigenvalue problem), 
                                                       system2 (a complex Hermitian standard eigenvalue problem),

                  -Those systems are solved using the different feast_dense, feast_banded, and feast_sparse drivers.
                  

                  -Here a list of the examples in both directories C and Fortran, while considering the system 
                          either dense, banded or sparse,
                          "s" denotes real single precision, "d" denotes real double precision
                          "c" denotes complex single precision, "z" denotes complex double precision

                           1_dense directory contains:
                           - helloworld (Solve the helloworld example presented in the documentation)
                           - {s,d}example_dense1   (solve matrix1- AX=eBX - real symmetric)
                           - {c,z}example_dense2   (solve matrix2- AX=eX  - Complex Hermitian)

                           2_banded directory contains:
                           - {s,d}example_banded1  (solve matrix1- AX=eBX - real symmetric)
                           - {c,z}example_banded2  (solve matrix2- AX=eX  - Complex Hermitian)

                           3_sparse directory contains:
                           - {s,d}example_sparse1  (solve matrix1- AX-eBX - real symmetric)
                           - {c,z}example_sparse2  (solve matrix2- AX=eX  - Complex Hermitian)

                     

